{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 2, :comments ["<b>Established.</b> And because he mentioned the earth, for it stands by the power of HaShem upon its foundation (mutsqa), which is the central point, and it itself is the point of the Throne of Glory, which is the encompassing line, therefore: <b>Your throne is established</b> [נכון כסאך מאז]. And because he mentioned that His throne stands, he said: <b>From eternity You are</b> [ומעולם אתה] — primordial, and there is no beginning to You, as if he said: from eternity You sit upon the throne."], :book :psalms, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 93, :notes {0 "Mutsqa (מוצקה) rendered 'foundation' based on context; the term relates to the earth's foundational or poured-solid base in medieval cosmological discussions."}, :source-witnesses [["Ibn Ezra on Psalms -- Daat" "http://www.daat.ac.il/he-il/tanach/parshanut_hamikra/full-text/eben-ezra/tehilim"] ["Wikisource Mikraot Gedolot" "http://en.wikisource.org/wiki/Mikraot_Gedolot/"] ["Tanakh, Venice, 1617-1619" "https://dlib.rsl.ru/viewer/01007514045#?page=4"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T19:37:07.470973782Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}